\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 How it works\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The gadget is only a remote with a face. The real "Jarvis" is an AI agent running on a computer or server, and the gadget just carries your words to it and shows the reply.\
There are three parts:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The device.
\f1\b0  An ESP32 board with a screen, a mic and buttons. It shows a pet, records your voice or reads a button press, and sends that over Wi\uc0\u8209 Fi.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The bridge.
\f1\b0  A small plugin, or a tiny web server, that runs next to the agent. It receives what the device sends and passes it to the agent, then returns the answer in a short form the device can draw.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The brain.
\f1\b0  The agent (Hermes Agent in the reel). It holds the memory, tools and AI model, and it decides what to say or do.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The device reaches the bridge in one of three ways, tried in order: home Wi\uc0\u8209 Fi, then Bluetooth to the PC as a backup, then Tailscale when you're away from home.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 [embed: node/95d1c63a-0721]\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

